.TH "easel alimerge" 1 "@EASEL_DATE@" "Easel @EASEL_VERSION@" "Easel Manual"

.SH NAME
easel alimerge \- merge alignments based on their reference (#=GC RF) annotation


.SH SYNOPSIS

.B easel alimerge
[\fIoptions\fR]
.I msafile1
[\fImsafile2\fR ...]


.SH DESCRIPTION

.PP
.B easel alimerge
reads two or more input alignments, merges them into a single
alignment according to shared consensus column annotation, and outputs the result.
For example,
.B easel alimerge
allows merging of MSAs that have been generated by
HMMER or Infernal searches with the same profile or CM against
different target sequence databases.

.PP
The input alignments must all be in Stockholm format. Each input file
may contain one or more MSAs, and all MSAs across all input files are
merged. Every MSA must have reference
.RB ( "#=GC RF" )
annotation to mark consensus versus insertion columns, and the
.B RF
annotation must be identical in all MSAs for nongap consensus positions.

.PP
The merge is accomplished by inserting additional all-gap columns in
each individual MSA as needed to bring their consensus RF annotation
into alignment. The added gap characters are usually '.' characters,
but can be '~' characters to satisfy two conventions of HMMER and
Infernal alignment (fragment marking, and local structure alignment).

.PP
If the output format is Stockholm or Pfam, annotation is transferred
from the input alignments to the merged alignment as follows. All
per-sequence
.RB ( "#=GS" )
and per-residue
.RB ( "#=GR" )
annotation is transferred. Per-file
.RB ( "#=GF" )
annotation is transferred when it is present and identical in all
alignments. Per-column
.RB ( "#=GC" )
annotation is transferred when it is present and identical in all
alignments at the consensus columns, and contains no non-gap
characters in insert columns. Annotation that fails these tests is
silently dropped from the merged alignment.

.PP
By convention from HMMER and Infernal, residues in an insertion block
are split-justified: residues from the first half of the block are
flushed left, and residues from the second half are flushed right.
In Infernal-style MSAs, 
local structure
.B "~"
columns in
.B RF
and
.B SS_cons
annotation are kept on the left of the insertion block, ahead
of regular insertion residues. Fragment-marking terminal
.B "~"
characters (used by HMMER and Infernal to flag 
fragments) are preserved at the ends of fragmented sequences.

.PP
With the
.B \-\-small
option,
.B easel alimerge
operates in memory-saving mode. The required RAM is then minimal
(typically only a few Mb) and independent of the alignment sizes. To
use
.BR \-\-small ,
all alignments must be in Pfam format (non-interleaved, 1
line/sequence Stockholm format). You can reformat alignments to Pfam
using
.BR "easel reformat" .
Without
.BR \-\-small ,
the required RAM is roughly the size of the final merged alignment,
which will necessarily be at least the summed size of all input
alignment files and is sometimes several times larger. If you are
merging large alignments, or experiencing slow performance, try
reformatting to Pfam and using
.BR \-\-small .

.PP
If
.I msafile
is
.BR \- ,
the alignments are read from
.IR stdin .
Reading from
.I stdin
is not allowed with
.BR \-\-small ,
which requires multiple passes over each input file.

.PP
MSAs are parsed in Easel's "text mode", independent of what alphabet
they are using (e.g. amino|DNA|RNA); all ASCII characters in the input
MSAs are preserved exactly.


.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B \-h
Print brief help; includes version number and a summary of all
options.

.TP
.BI \-o " f"
Output the merged alignment to file
.I f
instead of to
.IR stdout .

.TP
.B \-v
Be verbose. Print a per-MSA summary table to
.I stdout
(file number, file name, alignment number within that file, number of
sequences, number of columns, running total number of sequences, and
number of columns required in the merged alignment), and a report of
which per-file and per-column annotations were transferred to the
merged alignment.
This option can only be used in combination with
.BR \-o ,
so that the printed summary info is separate from the output alignment.

.TP
.B \-\-rfonly
Only include columns that are not gaps in the
.B "#=GC RF"
annotation in the merged alignment. The merged alignment then has
exactly as many columns as consensus columns marked by
.BR RF .
All inserted residues are discarded.

.TP
.B \-\-small
Operate in memory-saving mode. Required RAM is independent of the
sizes of the alignments to merge, instead of being roughly the size of
the eventual merged alignment. When enabled, all alignments must be in
Pfam Stockholm (non-interleaved, 1 line/seq) format; see
.BR "easel reformat" .
The output alignment is written in Pfam format.
Reading from
.I stdin
is not supported with
.BR \-\-small ,
because multiple passes over each input file are required.
Incompatible with
.BR \-\-outformat
(because output is essentially verbatim, Pfam format to Pfam format).

.TP
.BI \-\-outformat " fmt"
Write the merged alignment in alignment format
.IR fmt .
Choices for
.I fmt
are
.BR a2m|a3m|afa|clustal|clustallike|pfam|phylip|phylips|psiblast|selex|stockholm .
.I fmt
is case-insensitive (e.g.
.B afa
or
.BR AFA
both work). Default is
.BR stockholm .
Incompatible with
.BR \-\-small .


.SH SEE ALSO

.B man easel
for more information about Easel miniapps, their shared behaviors, and
some standardized options.

